# Headline pass-rate grid

**What this is.** One row per comparison tool, one column per SP6
RF label. The number inside each cell is the count of clusters in
which popout's estimate against that tool for that label cleared
the μ-gated pass criterion (Pearson r ≥ 0.95, CCC ≥ 0.90),
followed by the number of μ-evaluable clusters. **Green** ≥ 90%
pass; **yellow** 50–90%; **red** < 50%; **grey `μ·∅`** = every
cluster was μ-gated (no signal to evaluate).

**How to read this chart.** A row that is uniformly green says
popout agrees with that comparison tool across the cohort; a row
with red on a few RF labels says the disagreement is
label-specific. A row of grey cells says popout was never tested
against that tool in clusters where the label was prevalent
enough to assess.

